From: Boris Krasnovskiy <boris.krasnovskiy@ezurio.com>
Subject: [PATCH] camsys: camsv: fail stream-on when the top camsv is missing

camsv devices work in pairs and the DMA setup writes the even device's
(top) registers. If only the odd camsv is enabled in the DT, devs[] has
no top device and mtk_cam_sv_dev_config() oopses on a NULL drvdata.
Reject the pipe with -ENODEV and a message instead.

Signed-off-by: Boris Krasnovskiy <boris.krasnovskiy@ezurio.com>

Upstream-Status: Inappropriate [MediaTek out-of-tree driver]
---
diff --git a/drivers/media/platform/mtk-isp/isp_7x/camsys/src/mtk_cam-sv.c b/drivers/media/platform/mtk-isp/isp_7x/camsys/src/mtk_cam-sv.c
--- a/drivers/media/platform/mtk-isp/isp_7x/camsys/src/mtk_cam-sv.c
+++ b/drivers/media/platform/mtk-isp/isp_7x/camsys/src/mtk_cam-sv.c
@@ -884,6 +884,16 @@
 		return ret;
 	}
 
+	/* DMA setup goes through the pair's even "top" camsv, so it must be probed. */
+	for (i = 0; i < ARRAY_SIZE(sv->devs); i++) {
+		if ((sv_pipe->enabled_sv & 1<<i) && !sv->devs[i & ~1u]) {
+			dev_info(sv->cam_dev,
+				 "camsv%u needs camsv%u enabled in the DT\n",
+				 i + 1, (i & ~1u) + 1);
+			return -ENODEV;
+		}
+	}
+
 	for (i = 0; i < ARRAY_SIZE(sv->devs); i++) {
 		if (!(sv_pipe->enabled_sv & 1<<i))
 			continue;
